---
import CalculatorStyles from '../../components/calculators/CalculatorStyles.astro';
import FiberCalculator from '../../components/calculators/FiberCalculator';
import EmailSignup from '../../components/EmailSignup.astro';
import RecipeCard from '../../components/RecipeCard.astro';
import ToolShell from '../../components/ToolShell.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getRecipes } from '../../lib/recipes';

const title = 'Fiber calculator: daily guideline by age';
const description =
  'See the general daily fiber guideline for healthy people by age and sex, with an optional calorie-based figure for adults. Free, in grams.';

// Newest first. A production build may have no published recipes yet: then nothing renders.
const recipes = (await getRecipes()).slice(0, 3);
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <CalculatorStyles />
  <ToolShell
    title="Fiber calculator"
    purpose="Enter an age and sex to see the general daily fiber guideline for healthy people. Adults can add their calories for a second figure."
  >
    <FiberCalculator client:visible resultId="fc-result" />
    <noscript>
      <p>This calculator needs JavaScript. The explanation and the tables behind it are written out below.</p>
    </noscript>
    <div slot="result" id="fc-result">
      <p>Your guideline will appear here once you enter an age and choose a sex.</p>
    </div>
    <Fragment slot="source">
      <p>
        This is a general guideline for healthy people, not medical or dietary advice. Talk to a doctor or registered
        dietitian about your own needs.
      </p>
    </Fragment>
  </ToolShell>

  <section class="prose rc-about" aria-labelledby="how-h">
    <!-- TODO(dietitian): review before launch -->
    <h2 id="how-h">How to use it</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Enter an age in whole years, 4 or over, and choose female or male.</li>
      <li>The first figure is the Adequate Intake for that age and sex.</li>
      <li>Adults aged 19 and over can also enter their calories a day to see a second, separate figure.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2 id="two-h">Two figures, two bases</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Adequate Intake by age and sex.</strong> The first figure is the Adequate Intake (AI) for total fiber
      from the Food and Nutrition Board of the National Academies (IOM), in Dietary
      Reference Intakes for Energy, Carbohydrate, Fiber, Fat, Fatty Acids, Cholesterol, Protein, and Amino Acids
      (2002/2005). The Board's table note says the AI is believed to cover the needs of all healthy individuals in the
      groups. Its values are 25 g a day for ages 4 to 8; 31 g (male) and 26 g (female) for ages 9 to 13; 38 g and 26 g
      for ages 14 to 18; 38 g and 25 g for ages 19 to 30 and 31 to 50; and 30 g and 21 g for ages 51 to 70 and over 70.
      The source table is the
      <a
        href="https://www.nationalacademies.org/index.php/cdn/materials/9fb9fae6-337c-4b7c-9821-2c81d1f65ad0"
        rel="noopener">DRI summary table (National Academies)</a
      >, which is marked as a prepublication copy with uncorrected proofs.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>14 g per 1,000 calories.</strong> The second figure is 14 g of fiber for every 1,000 kcal you enter,
      rounded to the nearest gram. This basis appears in Appendix 1 of the
      <a
        href="https://www.dietaryguidelines.gov/sites/default/files/2020-12/Dietary_Guidelines_for_Americans_2020-2025.pdf"
        rel="noopener">Dietary Guidelines for Americans, 2020-2025</a
      >. The 2025-2030 edition does not give a gram target for fiber.
    </p>
    <p>
      The two figures can differ. The IOM table gives one value for each age and sex group, while the Dietary Guidelines
      apply 14 g per 1,000 kcal at fixed calorie levels, so the calorie level each one assumes is likely part of the
      reason. Neither is a target set for you.
    </p>

    <h2 id="adding-h">Adding fiber</h2>
    <p>
      NIH MedlinePlus advises adding fiber gradually, over a period of a few weeks, and drinking water with it
      (<a href="https://medlineplus.gov/ency/article/002470.htm" rel="noopener">MedlinePlus, fiber in diet</a>).
    </p>

    <h2 id="limits-h">What it does not do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>It covers ages 4 and over only. There are no values for younger children, pregnancy or breastfeeding.</li>
      <li>
        The calorie range of 1,000 to 4,000 kcal a day is this site's own limit. It does not come from the sources.
      </li>
      <li>The calorie-based figure is only given for ages 19 and over. The Adequate Intake never depends on calories.</li>
      <li>
        This is a general guideline for healthy people, not medical or dietary advice. Talk to a doctor or registered
        dietitian about your own needs.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  {
    recipes.length > 0 && (
      <section class="no-print" aria-labelledby="recipes-h">
        <h2 id="recipes-h">Recipes to try</h2>
        <ul class="grid">
          {recipes.map((r) => (
            <li>
              <RecipeCard id={r.id} recipe={r.data} />
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </section>
    )
  }
  <EmailSignup />
</BaseLayout>
